{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI completed the full TDD workflow for the MHPCO Claim Office kata:\n\n- **Test List**: Created 39 tests in `src/claim-office.spec.ts` covering every rule and example from the spec (base premiums, component blocks, curse/enchantment surcharges, loyalty/first-insurance/follow-up modifiers, rounding rules, claim payouts, deductibles, cap tracking, dragon-material and high-enchantment clauses, and CLI error edge cases).\n- **Red/Green/Refactor**: Ran 39 Red→Green→Refactor cycles (several Red phases discovered the test already passed due to earlier generalization, correctly documented as \"already passes\" per the skill instructions). Each Green phase used the minimal implementation needed, and each Refactor phase was delegated to the isolated `refactor` subagent, which consistently evaluated naming first, applied the Simple Design Rules in priority order, and computed APP mass before/after each change.\n- **Implementation**: Built out `src/claim-office.ts` with a clean, well-named set of pure functions (`computeQuotePremium`, `computeClaimResult`, `sumBasePremiums`, `itemSurcharge`, `payoutForDamage`, `policyCap`, `validateDamagesAgainstPolicy`, etc.) and `src/cli.ts` as the required CLI entry point that reads JSON from stdin, calls `runScenario`, writes JSON to stdout, and exits non-zero with an error message to stderr on invalid input.\n- **Verification**: All 39 tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` is clean, and manual CLI smoke tests (schema example, unknown-item-type rejection, empty-list edge case) behave as specified.\n\nFinal marker file `experiment-done.txt` containing `DONE` has been written."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":659,"output":613,"cacheRead":176623,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":177895,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","times