mium for a quote's items (sum of base premiums, surcharge, fee, rounding). Name accurately reflects current behavior. Keep as is.\n- `runScenario`: still accurately describes iterating steps and dispatching per op type. Keep as is.\n- Inline stub `{ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 }` had no name at all — it's an anonymous magic value that reads as if it were a real computed result. This is the clarity gap I addressed.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (before refactor, the claim branch of `runScenario`):\n```ts\nreturn { payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 };\n```\n- Constants: 2 (`0`, `0`) = 2\n- Bindings: 0\n- Invocations: 0\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass: 2\n\n**Refactoring Applied** (Rule 2: Reveals Intent):\nExtracted the inline stub into a named constant `NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED_CLAIM_RESULT` with a comment explaining *why* it exists (claim rules aren't test-driven in yet). Previously, `{ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 }` looked like a legitimately computed result buried in the `map` callback — nothing signaled it was a temporary placeholder. A future reader (or the next Red phase) could easily mistake it for real logic instead of an intentional TDD stub.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```ts\nconst NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED_CLAIM_RESULT: ClaimResult = { payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 };\n...\nreturn NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED_CLAIM_RESULT;\n```\n- Constants: 2 (`0`, `0`) = 2\n- Bindings: 1 (the named constant) = 1\n- Invocations: 0\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass: 3 (was 2, delta +1)\n\nPer the guidelines, **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP** — the +1 mass from naming the placeholder is a worthwhile trade for making an implicit \"not implemented yet\" stub explicit and self-documenting.\n\nRules 3 (No Duplication) and 4 (Fewest Elements) were also checked: no duplication exists in this small file, and no unnecessary abstractions were found elsewhere — `computeQuotePremium` remains a single, minimal, well-named function.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted the claim-step stub `{ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 }` into a named, commented constant `NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED_CLAIM_RESULT` to make its placeholder intent explicit (Rule 2: Reveals Intent).\n**Mass Change**: 2 -> 3 (+1, accepted because clarity trumps APP)\n**Tests**: All 2 passing tests still green (`NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` confirmed)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-24-53_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 2\nRecent Green phase: Added computeQuotePremium(items) that sums base premiums (currently only \"sword\": 100 defined), applies a 10% first-insurance surcharge, adds the processing fee, and rounds up (with a floating-point precision guard using Math.round(x*1e6)/1e6 before Math.ceil). runScenario now maps over steps, calling computeQuotePremium for quote steps and returning a stub {payout:0, remainingCap:0} for claim steps.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 2\nRecent Green phase: Added computeQuotePremium(items) that sums base premiums (currently only \"sword\": 100 defined), applies a 10% first-insurance surcharge, adds the processing fee, and rounds up (with a floating-point precision guard using Math.round(x*1e6)/1e6 before Math.ceil). runScenario now maps over steps, calling computeQuotePremium for quote steps and returning a stub {payout:0, remainingCap:0} for claim steps.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784917702486},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_018neSrWRfgo1TJojSgxuGw1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_011ToT3wi6xUrnUXdix6BVo9","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":330,"output":124,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10222,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784917702506,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0b5e647f-693c-4356-bf88-a29f301a86c3","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_018neSrWRfgo1TJojSgxuGw1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: QuoteItem[];\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n};\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\n\nfunction computeQuotePremium(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  const basePremiumSum = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUM[item.type], 0);\n  const withFirstInsurance = basePremiumSum * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE);\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatError = Math.round((withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE) * 1e6) / 1e6;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatError);\n}\n\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult {\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      return { premium: computeQuotePremium(step.items) };\n    }\n    return { payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 };\n  });\n  return { results };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784917704652},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_011ToT3wi6xUrnUXdix6BVo9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for main items (single item, no modifiers, newcomer) ---\n  it(\"single sword, newcomer -> base premium 100 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"single amulet, newcomer -> base premium 60 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 71 G\");\n  it.todo(\"single staff, newcomer -> base premium 80 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 93 G\");\n  it.todo(\"single potion, newcomer -> base premium 40 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 49 G\");\n\n  // --- Component building block of 3 alike ---\n  it.todo(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium (no block)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block - block requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\");\n\n  // --- \"Alike\" components: exact type match required for block ---\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"cursed sword + plain amulet -> policy base premium 160 G; cursed surcharge 50 G (50% of cursed item's base premium only) -> 210 G before further modifiers and fee\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> both curse and high-enchantment surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 4 -> curse surcharge applies, no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G -> final premium 198 G (rounded up, in MHPCO's favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G -> final payout 350 G (rounded down, in MHPCO's favor)\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G (full reimbursement minus deductible)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Claim processing: enchantment threshold vs dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (both clauses apply; 50% rule wins, then deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (high-enchantment clause applies at threshold, then deductible)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon attack damages insured sword (500 G) and insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G (100 G deductible applies once per damaged item)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G, cap 4000 G\");\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon attack damages both swords; damages array has two sword entries -> each treated as separate damage with its own deductible\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"damages array has more entries of a type than policy covers (two sword damages, one sword insured) -> CLI exits non-zero, whole claim rejected\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers a sword and an amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G, cap 3200 G\");\n  it.todo(\n    \"cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G, premium with modifiers 165 G) -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers a sword and 3 runes (a block) -> insurance sum 1750 G (block discount affects premium only, not insurance sum)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"sword insured (cap 2000 G); two successive claims of 1500 G each -> first payout 1400 G, cap remaining 600 G; second payout 600 G, cap remaining 0 G (reduced to remaining cap)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"quote includes an item with unknown type (e.g. broomstick) -> CLI exits non-zero and writes error to stderr, no results written to stdout\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim r