UN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-24-53_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 33 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  6 passed | 33 todo (39)\n   Start at  18:38:42\n   Duration  165ms (transform 29ms, setup 0ms, collect 28ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 49ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918322959},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: Added `rune: 25` to `BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE`\n**Result**: All tests now pass (6 passing, 33 todo)\n**Approach**: Minimal — no block logic yet, just per-item base premium\n\nProceeding to Refactor phase."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01TQMapPHke39sNqvJBsJyhy","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent Green phase: Added \"rune\": 25 to BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE. Note that upcoming tests will require special \"block of 3 alike components\" pricing logic (3 runes = 60 G flat instead of 75 G), so component pricing will soon need more than a flat per-item lookup.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":779,"output":415,"cacheRead":52756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":53950,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784918322960,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-54e2c8ea-8a4d-4987-a12f-beb634a7aab6","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01TQMapPHke39sNqvJBsJyhy","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 6 tests still passing. Here's the refactoring report.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current function: `computeQuotePremium(items)` — computes base sum, applies first-insurance surcharge, adds fee, rounds/ceils.\n- Assessment: name still fits — it computes the full quote premium, and that hasn't changed with the `rune` entry added.\n- Decision: keep `computeQuotePremium` as-is. However, the inline `items.reduce(...)` expression computing base premiums doesn't have a name of its own, which matters because the upcoming \"block of 3 alike components\" test will need to replace that flat per-item lookup with grouping/counting logic. Left inline, that change would tangle new conditional/loop logic into `computeQuotePremium` itself.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (`computeQuotePremium`, before):\n```\nfunction computeQuotePremium(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  const basePremiumSum = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n  const withFirstInsurance = basePremiumSum * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE);\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatError =\n    Math.round((withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE) * FLOAT_ROUNDING_PRECISION) / FLOAT_ROUNDING_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatError);\n}\n```\n- Bindings: `items`, `basePremiumSum`, `sum`, `item`, `withFirstInsurance`, `roundedToAvoidFloatError` = 6\n- Invocations: `reduce`, `+` (lookup access not counted), `Math.round`, `Math.ceil` = 4 → 8\n- Constants: `0`, `1` = 2\n- Loops: `reduce` = 1 → 5\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 6 + 8 + 2 + 5 = 21\n\n**Rule 3 (No Duplication) / Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) applied**: Extracted the base-premium summation into its own function, `sumBasePremiums(items)`, with a comment documenting *why* it's separated now (to isolate the future block-pricing change from the surcharge/fee formula). This is a Rule 2 move (clarity of responsibility boundaries) done in anticipation of Rule 3 need (avoiding duplicated/tangled pricing logic once block pricing is introduced).\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (`computeQuotePremium` + `sumBasePremiums`, after):\n```\nfunction sumBasePremiums(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n}\n\nfunction computeQuotePremium(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  const basePremiumSum = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = basePremiumSum * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE);\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatError =\n    Math.round((withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE) * FLOAT_ROUNDING_PRECISION) / FLOAT_ROUNDING_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatError);\n}\n```\n- `sumBasePremiums`: bindings `items, sum, item` = 3; invocation `reduce` = 1→2; constant `0` = 1; loop = 1→5. Subtotal = 11\n- `computeQuotePremium`: bindings `items, basePremiumSum, withFirstInsurance, roundedToAvoidFloatError` = 4; invocations `sumBasePremiums, Math.round, Math.ceil` = 3→6; constant `1` = 1. Subtotal = 11\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 11 + 11 = 22 (delta +1)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Extracted `sumBasePremiums` as a named, single-purpose function separate from `computeQuotePremium`.\n- Mass increased slightly (21 → 22) due to one extra invocation at the call site — expected and acceptable per the APP guideline that Rule 2/3 clarity trumps minimal mass (Rule 4 is lowest priority).\n- Benefit isn't visible in current test behavior but sets up a clean seam: the next test (3 runes = 60 G block pricing) can change `sumBasePremiums` internals (grouping by type, counting alikes) without touching the surcharge/rounding logic in `computeQuotePremium`, avoiding future duplication/tangling.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `sumBasePremiums(items)` from `computeQuotePremium` to isolate the base-premium calculation ahead of upcoming block-pricing logic (Rule 2/3 improvement).\n**Mass Change**: 21 -> 22 (+1, acceptable per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 6 passing (verified via `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/e