_01NRStgnLMw5jwS5rJSFiVs3","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 7 tests pass.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `sumBasePremiums`\n- Function purpose: \"compute total base premium for a set of items, applying either per-item lookup or a flat block discount\"\n- Assessment: Name still fits — it does sum/compute base premiums; the block-of-3 check is an internal detail of *how* the sum is computed, not a separate concept the function's name needs to expose.\n- Decision: Keep `sumBasePremiums`. However, the inline block-check condition (`items.length === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE && items.every(...)`) had no name of its own, which obscured what it represented as a concept.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (inline condition, before refactor):\n```ts\nif (items.length === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE && items.every((item) => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type))) {\n  return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n}\n```\n- Bindings: `items`, `COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE`, `item`, `COMPONENT_TYPES` = 4\n- Constants: `COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM` = 1\n- Invocations: `.length` (property, not counted), `.every`, `.has` = 2\n- Conditionals: `if`, `&&` = 4 (treating `if` as 1 conditional unit; `&&` is part of the same conditional expression)\n- Total ≈ 4 + 1 + 4 + 4 = 13 (within `sumBasePremiums`)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Extracted the block-detection condition into a named predicate `isComponentBlockOfThree(items)`.\n- This applies **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: the condition now names the domain concept (\"is this a block-of-3 alike components\") instead of leaving it as an anonymous boolean expression embedded in an `if`.\n- It also sets up **Rule 3 (No Duplication)** in advance: the upcoming \"same type\" tests (mixed rune/moonstone) and \"two separate blocks\" tests will need to reuse/extend this exact check; having it isolated in one named function means that logic change happens in one place.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```ts\nfunction isComponentBlockOfThree(items: QuoteItem[]): boolean {\n  return items.length === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE && items.every((item) => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type));\n}\n\nfunction sumBasePremiums(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  if (isComponentBlockOfThree(items)) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n}\n```\n- `isComponentBlockOfThree`: bindings 4 + constant 0 + invocations 2 + conditional (implicit in `&&`, no `if`) → treated as boolean expression, mass ≈ 4+2 = 6 (no `if` mass since it's a direct return)\n- `sumBasePremiums`'s `if`: bindings 0, invocation `isComponentBlockOfThree()` = 2, conditional `if` = 4, plus reduce loop unchanged = 5+existing\n- Net mass is roughly unchanged (extraction doesn't remove operations, just names them) — from ~13 to ~6+4+2=12, essentially flat, with one added invocation offsetting the removed inline `&&`.\n\nMass Change: ~13 → ~12 (negligible delta; this refactor is justified by **Rule 2 (clarity)**, which takes priority over minor APP mass differences.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Renamed the inline condition into `isComponentBlockOfThree` for intent-revealing clarity and to prepare a single extension point for the upcoming \"same type\" and \"multiple blocks\" rules.\n\n**Tests**: All 7 passing, unchanged behavior confirmed via `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-24-53_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: Added block-of-3 pricing to sumBasePremiums: if the items array has exactly 3 items and all are component types (rune/moonstone), return a flat COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM (60G) instead of summing individual base premiums. Note: this check currently only verifies \"all are component types\" not \"all are the SAME type\" -- that distinction will be forced by upcoming tests about mixed rune/moonstone combos.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: Added block-of-3 pricing to sumBasePremiums: if the items array has exactly 3 items and all are component types (rune/moonstone), return a flat COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM (60G) instead of summing individual base premiums. Note: this check currently only verifies \"all are component types\" not \"all are the SAME type\" -- that distinction will be forced by upcoming tests about mixed rune/moonstone combos.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784918708546},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_018KMM3RvJcq7MQ9dC3FdL6U","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_016cRQTStVqj82zMmgFjgRYF","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":323,"output":117,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10208,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784918708568,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-85142842-1174-4ecd-974c-cc42e7d3058e","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_018KMM3RvJcq7MQ9dC3FdL6U","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: QuoteItem[];\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n};\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\n\n// Multiplier used to round to 6 decimal places before ceiling, avoiding\n// binary floating point artifacts (e.g. 114.99999999999999) that would\n// otherwise round the premium down to the wrong whole number.\nconst FLOAT_ROUNDING_PRECISION = 1e6;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\n// Sums the base premium for each item independently. This is currently a\n// flat per-item lookup, but is kept separate from the surcharge/fee formula\n// below because upcoming \"block of 3 alike components\" pricing rules will\n// need to change how items are priced without touching the rest of the\n// premium calculation.\nfunction sumBasePremiums(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  if (items.length === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE && items.every((item) => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type))) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n}\n\nfunction computeQuotePremium(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  const basePremiumSum = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = basePremiumSum * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE);\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatError =\n    Math.round((withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE) * FLOAT_ROUNDING_PRECISION) / FLOAT_ROUNDING_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatError);\n}\n\n// Claim processing is not implemented yet -- every claim step resolves to this\n// placeholder until the payout/remainingCap rules are test-driven in.\nconst NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED_CLAIM_RESULT: ClaimResult = { payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 };\n\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult {\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      return { premium: computeQuotePremium(step.items) };\n    }\n    return NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED_CLAIM_RESULT;\n  });\n  return { results };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918710602},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_016cRQTStVqj82zMmgFjgRYF","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for main items (single item, no modifiers, newcomer) ---\n  it(\"single sword, newcomer -> base premium 100 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet, newcomer -> base premium 60 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"single staff, newcomer -> base premium 80 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"single potion, newcomer -> base premium 40 G + 10% first insurance + 5 G fee = 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Component building block of 3 alike ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium (no block)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 50 G, +10% first insurance = 55, +5 fee = 60\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 60 G (block), +10% first insurance = 66, +5 fee = 71\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block - block requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\");\n\n  // --- \"Alike\" components: exact type match required for block ---\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"cursed sword + plain amulet -> policy base premium 160 G; cursed surcharge 50 G (50% of cursed item's base premium only) -> 210 G before further modifiers and fee\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> both curse and high-enchantment surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 4 -> curse surcharge applies, no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G -> final premium 198 G (rounded up, in MHPCO's favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G -> final payout 350 G (rounded down, in MHPCO's favor)\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G (full reimbursement minus deductible)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Claim processing: enchantment threshold vs dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (both clauses apply; 50% rule wins, then deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (hig