Tokens":75320,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784918996748,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-287174a0-d14f-4b5f-98cb-91ce64c4da22","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_015mRCh84NUyjBi6TLMbcmnA","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 11 tests pass. Refactoring report below.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `sumBasePremiums`\n- Function purpose: \"sums the base premium of a policy's items, applying block discounts per group of same-type items\"\n- Assessment: The name still accurately describes the top-level responsibility (summing base premiums across the whole item list). It reveals intent well; no rename needed.\n- The inline reducer callback previously embedded a second responsibility (pricing one group) inside `sumBasePremiums`'s reducer, which blurred what `sumBasePremiums` itself does vs. what \"pricing a single group\" means.\n\nDecision: Keep `sumBasePremiums`'s name, but extract the group-pricing logic into a separate, named function (`premiumForGroup`) so each function has one clear responsibility that its name fully captures.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (`sumBasePremiums` before):\n```ts\nfunction sumBasePremiums(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  return groupByType(items).reduce((total, group) => {\n    if (isComponentBlockOfThree(group)) {\n      return total + COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n    }\n    return total + group.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n  }, 0);\n}\n```\n- Bindings: `items`, `total`, `group`, `sum`, `item` = 5\n- Invocations: `groupByType`, `reduce` (outer), `isComponentBlockOfThree`, `reduce` (inner), lookup `BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[...]` = 5 → 10\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if`) = 4\n- Loops: 2 (`reduce` outer + inner) = 10\n- Constants: 1 (`0`) = 1\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass: 5 + 10 + 4 + 10 + 1 = **30**\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (`sumBasePremiums` + `premiumForGroup`):\n```ts\nfunction premiumForGroup(group: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  if (isComponentBlockOfThree(group)) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return group.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n}\n\nfunction sumBasePremiums(items: QuoteItem[]): number {\n  return groupByType(items).reduce((total, group) => total + premiumForGroup(group), 0);\n}\n```\n- `premiumForGroup`: bindings `group`, `sum`, `item` = 3; invocations `isComponentBlockOfThree`, `reduce`, lookup = 3 → 6; conditional = 4; loop = 5; constant `0` = 1 → subtotal 19\n- `sumBasePremiums`: bindings `items`, `total`, `group` = 3; invocations `groupByType`, `reduce`, `premiumForGroup` = 3 → 6; loop = 5; constant `0` = 1 → subtotal 15\n\nTotal Mass: 19 + 15 = **34**\n\nMass Change: 30 → 34 (delta +4)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Split the single nested reducer into two named functions: `sumBasePremiums` (iterates groups) and `premiumForGroup` (prices one group, block or per-item).\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) improvement outweighs the small APP mass increase: each function now has exactly one responsibility that its name fully describes, and the block-discount decision reads as a standalone, testable-in-isolation concept rather than an anonymous inline branch buried in a reducer.\n- No duplication introduced or removed (Rule 3 unaffected).\n- Element count increased by one function (Rule 4), but this is justified by the clarity gain per Rule 2 > APP > Rule 4 priority.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `premiumForGroup(group)` out of `sumBasePremiums`'s reducer to separate \"how to price one group\" from \"how to combine group prices,\" improving readability of both functions.\n**Mass Change**: 30 → 34 (+4, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 11 passing, 28 todo unaffected (`NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-24-53_claim-offi