ecent Green phase: computeQuotePremium now takes (customer, items) and applies a 20% loyalty discount on the policy base premium sum when customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 (LOYALTY_MIN_YEARS). runScenario passes scenario.customer through.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":1657,"output":429,"cacheRead":85987,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":88073,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919346912,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-7944a2c6-37ae-4f36-950a-0e47cbe8c2d6","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_0151BiktX7ih8v6W44Fb3ntk","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 13 tests pass. Here's the refactoring report.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `computeQuotePremium`\n- Function purpose: \"computes the total quote premium for a customer's items, applying base premiums, surcharges, first-insurance surcharge, and a loyalty discount\"\n- Assessment: Name still accurately reveals intent — no rename needed.\n- Other names checked: `sumBasePremiums`, `sumItemSurcharges`, `itemSurcharge`, `basePremiumFor`, `premiumForGroup`, `isComponentBlockOfThree`, `groupByType` — all still precisely describe current behavior.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (loyalty discount line, before refactor):\n```ts\nconst loyaltyDiscount =\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_MIN_YEARS ? basePremiumSum * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n```\n- Bindings: 3 (`customer`, `basePremiumSum`, `LOYALTY_MIN_YEARS` reference, `LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE` reference) → counted as 4 bindings = 4\n- Constants: 1 (`0`) = 1\n- Conditionals: 1 (ternary) = 4\n- Invocations: 0\nTotal mass: 9\n\n**Refactoring Applied — Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**:\nExtracted the loyalty-eligibility