implicit domain knowledge worth documenting since no more tests will pin it down further).\n\n### Initial APP Mass (relevant excerpt — `runScenario`)\n\n```js\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult {\n  const capUsedByPolicyIndex = new Map<number, number>();\n  let quoteStepsSeen = 0;\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstContract = quoteStepsSeen === 0;\n      quoteStepsSeen += 1;\n      return { premium: computeQuotePremium(scenario.customer, step.items, isFirstContract) };\n    }\n    return processClaimStep(step, scenario.steps, capUsedByPolicyIndex);\n  });\n  return { results };\n}\n```\n\n- Constants: `0`, `1` = 2\n- Bindings: `scenario`, `capUsedByPolicyIndex`, `quoteStepsSeen`, `results`, `step`, `isFirstContract` = 6\n- Invocations: `new Map`, `.map`, `computeQuotePremium`, `processClaimStep` = 4 → mass 8\n- Conditionals: `if (step.op === \"quote\")` = 1 → mass 4\n- Loops: `.map` = 1 → mass 5\n- Assignments: `quoteStepsSeen += 1` = 1 → mass 6\n\n**Total Mass: 2 + 6 + 8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 31**\n\n### Refactored Code Mass\n\n```js\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult {\n  const capUsedByPolicyIndex = new Map<number, number>();\n  let hasQuotedBefore = false;\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstContract = !hasQuotedBefore;\n      hasQuotedBefore = true;\n      return { premium: computeQuotePremium(scenario.customer, step.items, isFirstContract) };\n    }\n    return processClaimStep(step, scenario.steps, capUsedByPolicyIndex);\n  });\n  return { results };\n}\n```\n\n- Constants: `false`, `true` = 2\n- Bindings: `scenario`, `capUsedByPolicyIndex`, `hasQuotedBefore`, `results`, `step`, `isFirstContract` = 6\n- Invocations: `new Map`, `.map`, `computeQuotePremium`, `processClaimStep` = 4 → mass 8\n- Conditionals: `if`, plus the implicit negation `!hasQuotedBefore` counts as a boolean op not a branch = 1 → mass 4\n- Loops: `.map` = 1 → mass 5\n- Assignments: `hasQuotedBefore = true` = 1 → mass 6\n\n**Total Mass: 2 + 6 + 8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 31** (unchanged numerically — same shape of computation, just a clearer variable)\n\n### Other cleanup (Rule 2)\n\nAlso removed a now-stale forward-looking comment on `insuranceValueFor` that referenced \"per-item cap logic later\" — since this is the final refactor pass for the kata, that speculative future never arrives, and leaving the comment would mislead future readers into expecting unbuilt functionality.\n\n### Rules 3 & 4 (Duplication / Fewest Elements)\n\nReviewed the whole file for duplication and unnecessary abstraction:\n- `lookupItemTypeValue` is correctly shared between `basePremiumFor` and `insuranceValueFor` — no duplication.\n- `countByKey` is correctly shared between damage and policy counting — no duplication.\n- All extracted helpers (`isComponentBlockOfThree`, `groupByType`, `premiumForGroup`, etc.) are each used and each represent one clear concept — no unnecessary elements found to remove.\n- No dead code, unused exports, or redundant abstractions found.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `quoteStepsSeen` (counter) → `hasQuotedBefore` (boolean flag) to match its actual purpose; removed a stale forward-looking comment.\n**Mass Change**: 31 → 31 (no change — this was a pure clarity improvement, consistent with Rule 2 trumping APP mass)\n**Tests**: All 39 passing (`NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`)"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":902,"output":2082,"cacheRead":31262,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":34246,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784921719399,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-eeef74a3-a63a-4a6d-86ce-26834f411613","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":107005,"output":14330